---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '~/config/site';
import { breadcrumbSchema } from '~/lib/schema';

const breadcrumb = breadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home',                url: SITE.url + '/' },
  { name: 'Resources',           url: SITE.url + '/resources' },
  { name: 'Finances & Reserves', url: SITE.url + '/hoa-collections-delinquency' },
]);
---
<BaseLayout
  title="HOA Collections & Delinquency: A Board’s Guide — CMGT"
  description="How HOA boards keep delinquency low with a fair, consistent collections process — and why rising delinquency is a top reason boards switch managers."
  pageSchema={breadcrumb}
>
  <nav id="site-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb" data-crumbs='[{"t":"Home","href":"/"},{"t":"Resources","href":"/resources"},{"t":"Finances & Reserves"}]'></nav>

  <article>
    <header class="art-hero">
      <div class="container art-hero-in">
        <div class="art-cat">Finances &amp; Reserves</div>
        <h1 class="art-h1">Keeping HOA delinquency low — fairly.</h1>
        <p class="art-lede">Unpaid assessments don’t just dent the budget — they shift the burden onto neighbors who do pay. The fix isn’t harsher penalties. It’s a consistent, compassionate process everyone can see coming.</p>
        <div class="art-meta"><span>6 min read</span><span class="dot"></span><span>Updated June 2026</span></div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="art-body">
      <div class="container art-wrap">
        <div class="art-take reveal">
          <p class="art-take-h">The short version</p>
          <p class="art-take-p">Low delinquency comes from consistency, not aggression. A written policy applied the same way for everyone keeps the budget whole and the community fair — our communities average around 10%.</p>
        </div>
        <h2 class="art-h2">Why delinquency matters more than it looks</h2><p class="art-p">Every unpaid assessment is a hole in the budget that paying owners quietly cover. Let it grow and you get thinned reserves, deferred maintenance, and eventually a special assessment that punishes the responsible majority.</p><p class="art-p">Rising delinquency is also one of the two most common reasons boards fire their management company — right alongside poor communication.</p><h2 class="art-h2">Start with a written policy</h2><p class="art-p">A collections policy should spell out when an account is late, what happens at each stage (reminder, late fee, formal notice, lien, legal referral), and the timeline for each. Adopt it formally, share it with every owner, and — this is the part that matters — apply it identically to everyone.</p><p class="art-p">Selective enforcement is how boards end up in disputes. Consistency is the whole game.</p><h2 class="art-h2">Make paying the easy option</h2><p class="art-p">A surprising amount of delinquency is friction, not refusal. Online payments, autopay, clear statements, and reminders before the due date recover more than late fees ever will. Meet people where they are before you escalate.</p><h2 class="art-h2">Escalate calmly and consistently</h2><p class="art-p">When an account does go seriously past due, a documented, predictable escalation protects the community legally and keeps emotion out of it. The goal isn’t to punish a neighbor — it’s to protect everyone else’s investment. A steady process gets there without the drama.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <section class="rel">
    <div class="container">
      <h2 class="rel-h">Keep reading.</h2>
      <div class="rel-grid"><a class="rel-card" href="/hoa-financial-management"><span class="rel-t">HOA Financial Management</span><span class="rel-ar">→</span></a><a class="rel-card" href="/switching-hoa-management-companies"><span class="rel-t">Switching Managers</span><span class="rel-ar">→</span></a><a class="rel-card" href="/hoa-management-services"><span class="rel-t">Full-Service HOA Management</span><span class="rel-ar">→</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta">
    <div class="container cta-in">
      <div><h2 class="cta-h">Want this handled for you?</h2><p class="cta-p">A real person will walk through your community’s situation — within one business day.</p></div>
      <div><a class="btn btn-blue" href="/request-a-proposal">Request a proposal <span class="arrow">→</span></a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  body { background: #fff; }
  .eyebrow-blue { color: var(--freedom-blue); opacity: .6; }
  .art-hero { background: var(--nb-lightest); padding: 76px 0 64px; }
  .art-hero-in { max-width: 820px; }
  .art-cat { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 700; font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--landscaping-green); }
  .art-h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 60px); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.025em; color: var(--freedom-blue); margin: 16px 0 20px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .art-lede { font-size: clamp(17px, 2vw, 21px); line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-700); margin: 0 0 24px; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .art-meta { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-400); }
  .art-meta .dot { width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--hairline-strong); }
  .art-body { background: #fff; padding: 70px 0 100px; }
  .art-wrap { max-width: 720px; }
  .art-take { background: var(--fb-lightest); border-left: 4px solid var(--landscaping-green); border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0; padding: 24px 28px; margin: 0 0 44px; }
  .art-take-h { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 700; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .16em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--freedom-blue); opacity: .6; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .art-take-p { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--freedom-blue); margin: 0; }
  .art-h2 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(24px, 2.8vw, 32px); line-height: 1.18; letter-spacing: -.015em; color: var(--freedom-blue); margin: 44px 0 16px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .art-p { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink-700); margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .art-p strong { color: var(--freedom-blue); font-weight: 600; }
  .art-dl { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 22px; flex-wrap: wrap; background: var(--freedom-blue); color: #fff; border-radius: 16px; padding: 30px 32px; margin: 44px 0; }
  .art-dl-ico { flex: none; width: 56px; height: 56px; border-radius: 14px; background: rgba(255,255,255,.1); display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; color: var(--landscaping-green); }
  .art-dl-body { flex: 1; min-width: 200px; }
  .art-dl-t { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 21px; margin: 0 0 6px; }
  .art-dl-d { font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: rgba(255,255,255,.78); margin: 0; }
  .art-disclaimer { font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-400); border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline); padding-top: 20px; margin: 44px 0 0; font-style: italic; }
  .rel { background: var(--nb-lightest); padding: 90px 0; }
  .rel-h { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 36px); letter-spacing: -.015em; color: var(--freedom-blue); margin: 0 0 32px; }
  .rel-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 20px; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .rel-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .rel-card { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; background: #fff; border: 1.5px solid var(--hairline-strong); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 26px; text-decoration: none; transition: border-color var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out), transform var(--dur-base) var(--ease-out); }
  .rel-card:hover { border-color: var(--landscaping-green); transform: translateY(-2px); }
  .rel-t { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: 17px; color: var(--freedom-blue); }
  .rel-ar { color: var(--landscaping-green); font-size: 18px; }
  .cta { background: var(--landscaping-green); color: var(--freedom-blue); padding: 90px 0; }
  .cta-in { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 48px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .cta-h { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 50px); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.02em; margin: 0 0 10px; text-wrap: balance; }
  .cta-p { font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 460px; margin: 0; color: rgba(30,30,119,.82); }
</style>
